  data:  # 0fc2
    kind: work_item  # 0fc2
    title: "DDG builds no CFG for a function literal under a package-level var_spec: every INV-nopoh-anchored finding is structural-only (29 of 29 on beads)"  # 0fc2
    status: todo_hard  # 0fc2
    priority: 2  # 0fc2
    parent:  # 0fc2
    tags:  # 0fc2
    - go  # 0fc2
    - taint  # 0fc2
    - dataflow  # 0fc2
    isbefore: []  # 0fc2
    duplicate_of: []  # 0fc2
    not_duplicate_of: []  # 0fc2
    pr_ref:  # 0fc2
    description: "FILED 2026-09-03 with INV-nopoh's fix, which anchors a Go call under a\npackage-level `var` on the variable's own symbol (kind `variable`, span = the\nvar_spec). Measured on beads (taint arm A vs B, cold, generic-taint-claims):\n134 -> 162 flow rows; 29 added, and EVERY added row whose source is a\n`:variable` symbol (the cobra command variables: rootCmd, initCmd, doctorCmd,\nmigrateCmd, ...) carries analysis_method=structural. None can be DDG-adjudicated.\n\nWHY. `hypergumbo_lang_mainstream/go_def_use.py` registers\n    LanguageDdgSpec(function_node_types={\"function_declaration\", \"method_declaration\"}, ...)\nand `ddg_build` walks the tree for those node types, takes `child_by_field_name(\"body\")`,\nand names the CFG with make_symbol_id(lang, path, start, end, name, kind). A function\nliteral under a package-level var_spec is neither node type, so no CFG is built for\nits body; the taint walk finds no ddg_symbols entry for `go:...:23-425:migrateCmd:variable`\nand falls back to structural reachability. The edges exist now; the walk cannot run\nover them. (INV-muhij Finding B and section 3a are unaffected: nothing new gates a\nverdict.)\n\nWHAT WOULD FIX IT (design, not done):\n  1. Let the spec name a body for a var_spec whose initializer is (or contains, at\n     the struct-field position) a func_literal: `function_node_types` gains\n     \"var_spec\" restricted to package level, `name_for` returns the var name,\n     `kind_for` returns \"variable\", and a new optional `body_for(node)` hook returns\n     the literal's `body` (default: child_by_field_name(\"body\")). The id then matches\n     the analyzer's variable symbol EXACTLY (same span, same name, same kind) -- the\n     line-up constraint go_def_use.py's own header states.\n  2. A cobra handler `Run: func(cmd *cobra.Command, args []string) {...}` has\n     PARAMETERS; the CFG's parameter defs must come from the literal's\n     parameter_list, not the var_spec.\n  3. Two literals under one var (`var x = struct{A, B func()}{A: func(){}, B: func(){}}`)\n     share the anchor; the CFG should cover both bodies or the first and disclose.\n  4. Measure: re-run taint arm B on beads; the 29 structural rows should gain\n     ddg_mixed where the value actually flows, and the rows where it does NOT\n     (env read in one branch, print in another) should be refuted or forfeited\n     per WI-kabif's gate -- that is the point.\nSame gap will apply to each language fixed under the family item filed with INV-nopoh."  # 0fc2
    fields: {}  # 0fc2
- op: discuss  # 0982
  at: '2026-10-01T00:58:26Z'  # 0982
  by: agent  # 0982
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 0982
  clock: 2  # 0982
  nonce: '0982'  # 0982
  message: "PREMISE CHECK 2026-09-30 (dev 7f0f993843): CURRENT-WITH-UPDATES (fix design must change).\nHolds: go_def_use.py:310-316 still registers LanguageDdgSpec(function_node_types={\"function_declaration\",\"method_declaration\"}) only; file unchanged since 2026-09-03.\nLive repro (scratch Go file; var rootCmd = &Command{Run: func(args []string){ x := os.Getenv(\"A\"); fmt.Println(x) }} plus an equivalent func helper()): analyze_go anchors both calls on go:main.go:12-17:rootCmd:variable (span 12:4-17); build_repo_ddg(languages=(\"go\",), analyzer_symbols=analyzer_symbol_index(...)) -> ddg_symbols = {helper} only. The 29/29 beads figure was NOT re-measured.\nWhat changed since filing: WI-mufag (d878c955e4, 09-29) added LanguageDdgSpec.bound_callable_node_types -- a node is walked ONLY under the analyzer's own id at its exact span (ddg_build.py ~311-324; \"Callables Named by Their Binding\"), and LIVE.md records the rule \"THE DDG NEVER RE-DERIVES A NAME\". Only ts_def_use.py uses it.\nConsequence for this item's design step 1: having name_for return the var name and kind_for return \"variable\" is re-deriving the analyzer's name -- the thing WI-mufag ruled out. Route it through bound_callable_node_types instead. Two blockers there, both measured on the fixture:\n  a. analyzer_symbol_index (ddg_build.py:137) keeps only _CALLABLE_KINDS {function, method, getter, setter}; the `variable` anchor is dropped, so nothing would match.\n  b. The anchor's span is the var_spec (12:4), not the func_literal (13:6); a var_spec has no `body` field, so the body hook (the item's body_for) is still needed.\nSteps 2-4 (parameters from the literal, two literals under one var, measure on beads) stand."  # 0982
- op: update  # aba5
  at: '2026-10-01T01:36:21Z'  # aba5
  by: agent  # aba5
  actor: jgstern_agent  # aba5
  clock: 3  # aba5
  nonce: aba5  # aba5
  set:  # aba5
    description: "FILED 2026-09-03 with INV-nopoh's fix, which anchors a Go call under a package-level `var` on the variable's own symbol (kind `variable`, span = the var_spec). Measured on beads (taint arm A vs B, cold, generic-taint-claims): 134 -> 162 flow rows; 29 added, and EVERY added row whose source is a `:variable` symbol (the cobra command variables: rootCmd, initCmd, doctorCmd, migrateCmd, ...) carries analysis_method=structural. None can be DDG-adjudicated. (Not re-measured 2026-09-30.)\n\nWHY. `hypergumbo_lang_mainstream/go_def_use.py:310-316` registers\n    LanguageDdgSpec(function_node_types={\"function_declaration\", \"method_declaration\"}, ...)\nand no `bound_callable_node_types`. A function literal under a package-level var_spec is neither node type, so no CFG is built for its body; the taint walk finds no ddg_symbols entry for `go:...:23-425:migrateCmd:variable` and falls back to structural reachability. The edges exist; the walk cannot run over them.\n\nLive repro (2026-09-30, scratch main.go: `var rootCmd = &Command{Run: func(args []string){ x := os.Getenv(\"A\"); fmt.Println(x) }}` plus an equivalent `func helper()`): analyze_go anchors both calls on `go:main.go:12-17:rootCmd:variable` (span 12:4-17); `build_repo_ddg(languages=(\"go\",), analyzer_symbols=analyzer_symbol_index(...))` gives ddg_symbols = {helper} only.\n\nWHAT WOULD FIX IT (design, not done). The DDG never re-derives a name (WI-mufag, d878c955e4): a callable the analyzer names after its binding is walked ONLY under the analyzer's own id at its exact span, via `LanguageDdgSpec.bound_callable_node_types` (ddg_build.py, \"Callables Named by Their Binding\"; today used only by ts_def_use.py). A spec `name_for`/`kind_for` that rebuilds the var name and the `variable` kind would be a second copy of the analyzer's naming, so it is ruled out. Route Go through the WI-mufag mechanism instead; two blockers, both seen on the repro:\n  a. `analyzer_symbol_index` (ddg_build.py:137) indexes only `_CALLABLE_KINDS` {function, method, getter, setter}. The analyzer's anchor is kind `variable`, so it is dropped and nothing matches. The index must admit a `variable` symbol that anchors a function literal (and only that), without letting a plain data variable become a walked callable.\n  b. The anchor's span is the var_spec (12:4), not the func_literal (13:6), and a var_spec has no `body` field. Either list `var_spec` (package level only) as the bound node type and add an optional body hook returning the literal's `body`, or key the lookup from the literal to its enclosing var_spec's span. The id used must be the analyzer's, byte for byte.\nThen:\n  1. A cobra handler `Run: func(cmd *cobra.Command, args []string) {...}` has PARAMETERS; the CFG's parameter defs must come from the literal's parameter_list, not the var_spec.\n  2. Two literals under one var (`var x = struct{A, B func()}{A: func(){}, B: func(){}}`) share the anchor; the CFG should cover both bodies or the first and disclose.\n  3. Measure: re-run taint arm B on beads; the 29 structural rows should gain ddg_mixed where the value actually flows, and the rows where it does NOT (env read in one branch, print in another) should be refuted or forfeited per WI-kabif's gate -- that is the point.\nSame gap will apply to each language fixed under the family item filed with INV-nopoh.\nRevised 2026-09-30 from the premise check (see discussion)."  # aba5
- op: discuss  # a597
  at: '2026-10-01T19:10:27Z'  # a597
  by: agent  # a597
  actor: jgstern_agent  # a597
  clock: 4  # a597
  nonce: a597  # a597
  message: "WORK DONE 2026-10-01 (concurrent run), local branch jgstern-agent/fix/rovun, commit e38a67f806 (not pushed, not merged). Status NOT changed.\nPremise re-verified in code and live before the change: go_def_use registered function_declaration/method_declaration only; analyzer_symbol_index dropped kind `variable`; verify-claims (host_secret -> network) on \"read key, print len(key), send unrelated request\" read VIOLATED structural/unavailable as `var handler = func(...)` and as a cobra-style `Run:` field, while the same body as a declaration produced no evidence.\nFix (WI-mufag route, no name re-derivation): LanguageDdgSpec.bound_bodies_for (bound node = a BINDING holding bodies) + bound_anchor_kinds (non-callable kinds admitted to analyzer_symbol_index for that language only). Go: bound node var_spec, anchor kind variable, hook returns the OUTERMOST func_literal bodies of a PACKAGE-LEVEL var_spec (uses go.py _go_package_level_var_name, so local vars are excluded exactly as the analyzer excludes them). Each body is solved under the analyzer's id; stmt_defuse / unaccounted_names / hints merge per id (they were assigned, which would have kept only the last body). Item step 1 (parameters): a literal's parameters are not CFG definitions, exactly as a declaration's are not -- the CFG is built over the body in both cases; parity, nothing to add. Step 2 (two literals under one var): both bodies walked, and the id FORFEITS refutation, because two literals are two functions and a crossing value is cross-function. Also forfeits when the var holds a call outside every literal (Args: cobra.ExactArgs(1)).\nAfter the fix the live repro reads: var_literal and cobra_field LEAK = violated, analysis_method ddg / walk confirmed; NO_LEAK = no evidence (same as the declaration).\nMeasured on beads (generic-taint-claims, cold; arm A = git archive of origin/dev 135952dd34 run with ITS OWN measure script, arm B = this tree): situations sourced at a :variable anchor 27 (not 29 as filed) -- all structural/unavailable in A. In B: 1 ddg/confirmed, 2 ddg_mixed/escaped, 19 not_attempted cross_function, 4 source_not_tracked, 1 sink_before_source, 1 still structural (freshness.go debugPrintf: body has no DDG edges, which is also what a declaration gets). Total situations 303 -> 304 (compactCmd's 29-pair situation split into 1 ddg + 28 ddg_mixed), pair total 2080 = 2080, ZERO findings removed, every non-variable row unchanged. So on beads the effect is labels, not counts; the item's hoped-for refutations did not occur because the walk ran on only 3 of the 27.\nForfeit census on beads (Go DDG, this tree): 433 package-level variable symbols indexed, 129 walked (have edges), 119 forfeit refutation; with the binding gate switched off 109 forfeit by per-body coverage alone, so the gate itself forfeits 10 of 129.\nNOT done / residual: file-anchored sites (var _ = register(func(){...}), Python module-level code) are still not walked -- noted on WI-nilir with live repro."  # a597
